## Articles

- [Help to Buy: what it is, and what it is not](https://wombathomeloans.com.au/articles/help-to-buy-what-it-is/) - First home / government schemes
Help to Buy is the Australian Government shared-equity scheme. From 1 July 2026 the taxable income cap is $103,000 single or $165,000 joint or single parent. Deposit from 2%. Government contributes up to 30% (existing) or 40% (new). 10,000 places a year.
It is not the 5% deposit scheme. That scheme has no income cap and unlimited places. You own 100%. Help to Buy cannot be stacked with it.
Most high earners will not qualify. Book a 30-minute strategy session: https://wombathomeloans.com.au/book/

- [Deposit bonds for first home buyers: how they work at auction (and what they do not replace)](https://wombathomeloans.com.au/articles/deposit-bond-first-home/) - First home / deposit
A deposit bond is a digital certificate: a promise to pay the vendor at settlement, not cash leaving your account today.
It is not a home loan, not genuine savings, and not the funds you use to settle. The vendor does not have to accept it.
Auction and house hunting are the first-home door. The years-ahead developer bond is for people who already own. Book a 30-minute strategy session: https://wombathomeloans.com.au/book/

